n...(Interruptions)... It is a serious  \n\n336 \nmatter. The Minister has admitted the seriousness of it. \n...(Interruptions)... आप दे �खए ...(व्यवधान)... नह�ं, नह�ं, पा�ण जी, \n...(व्यवधान)... नह�ं, नह�ं ...(व्यवधान)... हमने दे खा है। ...(व्यवधान)... The House \nhas taken it seriously. ...(lnterrup- tions)... आप जाइए, प्ल�ज़। \n...(व्यवधान)... आप जाइए। ...(व्यवधान)... आप बै�ठए। The matter has been \nallowed to be raised. ...(Interruptions)... The matter has been allowed \nto be raised, and the hon. Home Minister has responded to it. \n...(Interruptions)... He has assured the House that if action is needed, \nit will be taken. Beyond that nothing can be said. ...(Interruptions)... \nThe privilege notice has also been given. That is under the consideration \nof the Chairman. ...(Interruptions)... You see, what all steps had to be  \ntaken have been taken. ...(Interruptions)... \nSHRI PRAKASH JAVADEKA (Maharashtra): No steps have been taken. \n...(Interruptions)... \nMR. DEPUTY CHAIRMAN: I mean, here in the House. ...(Interruptions)... \nश्रीमती सुषमा स्वराज (मध्य प्रदे श): सर, मुझे यह कहना है �क जैसी यह घटना थी, उस पर \nहोना तो यह चा�हए था �क गृह मंत्री जी Suo motu statement लेकर आते और सदन को बताते। \nले�कन हमारे कहने के बाद भी इन्ह�ने इस चीज़ को िजतना लाइटल� �लया है, हम इससे कतई संतुष्ट \nनह�ं ह� और हम सदन से ब�हर्गमन करते ह�। \n(तत्पश्चात ् कु छ सदस्य सदन से उठकर बाहर चले गए) \nMR. DEPUTY CHAIRMAN: He has not taken it lightly. He has taken it \nseriously. Now, Shrimati Brinda Karat. \nAlleged threat to women and young couples on Valentine's day \nSHRIMATI BRINDA KARAT (West Bengal): Sir, I would have been very happy \nif my friends would have just waited to hear this because concerns them \nin very direct way. In any case, Sir, I wish to draw the attention of the \nHouse to threats emanating from a group which calls itself the Rama Sene. \nIt would have been better, if they call themselves as Duryodhana Sena or \nthe Dushashan Sena. \nSHRI SITARAM YECHURI (West Bengal): No, the Ravana Sena. \nSHRIMATI BRINDA KARAT: 'Ravana', in any case, has got some other \nqualities, so I would not associate that with them. Sir, this is \npertaining to the fact that tomorrow happens to be February 14th, and \n\n337 \nsome young people in this country choose to observe the Saint Valentine's \nDay to express their love for each other. This Sena has threatened that \nany such couple seen, in any place, outside their homes, will be forcibly \nmarried, or, the girl will be forced to tie a rakhi onto the boy's hand, \netc. Now, really, Sir, we need not have taken such threats seriously had \nit not been for the fact that these threats have been preceded by the \nmost wild, savage and cowardly attacks. Series of attacks in the \nMangalore region of Karnataka on young women and particularly targeting \nthose young women who happen to be in the company of Muslim men. \nYesterday, we read in the paper that a young  \ngirl  committed  suicide because she was dragged out of her bus along \nwith an acquaintance of hers,  \n\n338 \nthreatened, humiliated, beaten, dragged to the police station, berated in \npublic, and then she was so humiliated that she committed suicide. Sir, \nthis boy has been arrest ed, accused of rape and we have no doubt about \nthis that this has happened only because that boy happens to be a Muslim. \nNone of those who dragged them off the bus have been arrested. \nEarlier, exactly the same thing happened to the daughter of a CPI MLA, \nwho was travelling by a bus. She was forcibly abducted off the bus, taken \nto a place, beaten up, threatened and only let off when she gave an \nassurance that she would not be seen speaking to the Muslim boy. The \nLeader of the Opposition has said that this is a perilous path for the \nRepublic to take. This is a perilous path because the truth of the matter \nis that this Hindutva twin of the Taliban, gets its inspiration from the \nsectarian agenda of the Hindutva forces at a Hindutva platform. \nThis is further strengthened by the fact that today, if this is made \npossible, it is because of the connivance of the very Government which is \nthere, sworn in in the name of the Indian Constitution. Therefore, Sir, \nthis is not just a question of this or that girl. \nThen, earlier, the girls who were in a pub, they are adult young \nwomen; they choose to go to a pub. There is no prohibition in Karnataka. \nThere is no law against this. Anybody can go to a pub if she so chooses. \nThey were dragged, beaten in public. I say, Sir, this is an affront to a \nfree and democratic India, it is a slap in the face of our democracy. The \nresponsibility of this is primarily with the Hindutva brigade. I would \nrepeat that it is the twin of Taliban. Therefore, since the State \nGovernment has refused to act, we demand that these organisations should \nbe proscribed under the sections of the new Act which has been recently \nadopted—the Unlawful Activities Prevention Act. And, tomorrow, the \nCentral Government must take up the responsibility to ensure the safety \nof our young women. \nSHRI DIGVIJAY SINGH (Jharkhand): Sir, I associate myself with the hon. \nMember. ...(Interruptions)... \nMR. DEPUTY CHAIRMAN: Yes, all associate. Now, Shri Thirunavukkarasar. \nDemand to take steps to restore peace and normalcy in Sri Lanka \nSHRI SU. THIRUNAVUKKARASAR (Madhya Pradesh): Sir, thank you very much \n\n339 \nfor allowing me to raise a very important matter. Sir, innocent \nTamilians, hundreds of them, in Sri Lanka are killed by the Sri Lankan \narmy for the past one month. Nearly 3 lakh Sri Lankan Tamils are \nwandering in the jungles without proper food, clothing and medicine. The \nSri Lankan army is chasing them everyday. Sri Lankan army and navy have \nalmost pushed them to the forest. Tamil Nadu Assembly has passed a \nresolution. All party leaders from Tamil Nadu, under the leadership of \nTamil Nadu Chief Minister, have come here and met the Prime Minister and \nthe External Affairs Minister. On behalf of the Government,  it  was  \npromised that Shri Pranab Mukherjee would be sent to Sri Lanka. It took \nnearly  \n\n340 \none month for him to go there. Even after that, the Tamil Nadu Chief \nMinister has mentioned in the press meeting that he was not informed \nabout the results of the talks between the two countries, between the two \nMinisters. The Central Government has, so far, done nothing. Moreover, \nIndian Government, it is reported in all the newspapers, is helping the \nSri Lankan Government. Two days back, the Sri Lankan President Rajapakse \nhas thanked the Indian Government for helping the Sri Lankan Government \nin this regard. \nSir, innocent people are being killed. Bombing is being done on \nhospitals, innocent sick people are being killed. This is the situation \nprevailing over there. \nAll the human rights are violated, Press people are not allowed there, \nthe Red Cross Society is not allowed there, international forums like the \nHuman Rights Commission are not allowed to inspect the affected areas. \nThey are not allowed to meet the affected people also. This is a very \nserious situation. All over the world people are agitated. (Time- bell). \nIn Tamil Nadu lot of youngsters, starting from one Muttukumarswamy, so \nmany have burnt themselves to death. The people are agitated but this \nGovernment is sleeping, it is not doing anything at all. The Tamil people \nshould be saved. The Indian Government should not help the Sri Lankan \nGovernment, it should not give any military aid and the Indian Government \nshould withdraw all the radars, which were already supplied, and this \nmatter should be immediately taken up in the UNO. The Central Government. \n...(Interruptions)... \nMR. DEPUTY CHAIRMAN: Shri D. Raja. ...(Interruptions)... Three minutes \nare over. ...(Interruptions)... \nSHRI SU. THIRUNAVUKKARASAR: Sir, the Central Government should take up \nthis matter with the Sri Lankan Government. \nSHRI D. RAJA (Tamil Nadu): Sir, the situation in Sri Lanka, as \nmentioned by my previous speaker, is very grave. There is a grave \nhumanitarian crisis threatening the lives of almost 300,000 Sri Lankan \nTamils. This issue should not be the concern of Tamil people alone; it \nshould be the concern of the entire nation. Even a party like the DMK, \nwhich is part of the UPA, an important ally of the UPA, has termed what \nis going on in Sri Lanka 'is nothing but a genocide'. So, it is \n\n341 \ngenocide , according to the DMK, according to an important ally of the \nUPA. If that is so, what is the response of India? I think, India has got \na moral and ethical responsibility because India is not just a neighbour \nto Sri Lanka, but India and Sri Lanka have got several bilateral \nagreements. India cannot be a mute spectator. But what is happening today \nis very disturbing. The Indian Government is supporting Sri Lankan \nmilitary in its war, India is sending more than 250 experts in radar and \nmodern surveillance technologies to Sri Lanka and India is also providing \ncontinuous satellite images of the Northern areas thereby providing a \ntactical edge to Sri Lankan Army and Air Force for precision in bombing  \nof  civilians  locations.  Indian  Navy  is  providing sea cover by \nmaking available all naval intelligence. I  \n\n342 \nwould like to ask what is the policy of the Government of India. If there \nis a policy, it is high time you recast your policy towards Sri Lanka. If \nyou have a policy, I think, that policy is to collaborate the war in Sri \nLanka, that is what is happening on ground. It so happens that there is \nconfusion in India's foreign policy as far as Sri Lanka is concerned. \nIndian Government considers that what is going on in Sri Lanka is a war \nbetween Sri Lankan Government and the LTTE; it is an internal problem of \nanother sovereign nation, so, India has a limited role. But I wish to \nunderline that India cannot treat this problem just as an internal \nproblem of a sovereign nation. We have more than 70 to 80 thousand \nrefugees in Tamil Nadu. Who is responsible for these refugees? What is \nthe policy of the UPA Government? The UPA Government is making a goody-\ngoody statement whereas this Government has miserably failed to safeguard \nthe lives of the innocen t Sri Lankan Tamils. My humble request is that \nthe Government comes up clean on its foreign policy towards Sri Lanka. I \nam asking the Rajapaksa Government to stop this war and find out a \npolitical solution to the problem. ...(Interruptions)... (Time- bell \nrings) \nMR. DEPUTY CHAIRMAN: Mr. Raja. ...(Interruptions)... Mr. Maitreyan, \nyou have not given your name. ...(Interruptions)... Are you supporting \nit? ...(Interruptions)... \nDR. V. MAITREYAN (Tamil Nadu): Sir, I will take only 30 seconds. \nDR. V. MAITREYAN: The attack on Tamilians in Sri Lanka is a matter of \nserious concern. The war has to be stopped. The fatal attack by the Sri \nLankan Army has to be stopped. In these efforts, whatever steps the \nCentral Government takes AIADMK will definitely support. \n...(Interruptions)... \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF PARLIAMENTARY AFFAIRS AND THE \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF PLANNING (SHRI V. NARAYANASAMY): I \nwould like to submit that, yesterday, the hon. President of India made it \nvery clear about the Indian Government's policy on Sri Lanka. The hon. \nPresident very clearly said that there should be ceasefire and they \nshould go to the negotiating table. ...(Interruptions)... \nSHRI DIGVIJAY SINGH (Jharkhand): Sir, hospitals are bombarded. \n...(Interruptions)... \nSHRI V. NARAYANASAMY: One thing I would like to say, Sir, at any cost \nour country. ...(Interruptions)...They have been kept as hostages by the \n\n343 \nLTTE militants. Our Government will not support the banned organisation, \nLTTE ...(Interruptions)... \nMR. DEPUTY SPEAKER: Please sit down. ...(Interruptions)... \nSHRI D. RAJA: Government of India cannot behave like this. \n...(Interruptions)... \nMR. DEPUTY SPEAKER: Mr. Raja, please sit down. \nReturning of medals by ex-army officers \nसरदार तरलोचन �स ंह (ह�रयाणा): �डप्ट� चेयरमैन सर, म� एक बहुत जरूर� मसले क� ओर आपका \nऔर  \nसारे  हाऊस  का ध्यान �दलाना चाहता हूं। 9 फरवर� को हमारे दे श के तकर�बन 300 �रटायडर् फौजी \nजरनल और वे  \n\n344 \nफौजी, िजन्ह� बहुत से अवाड्र्स �मले ह� एवं उनक� पित्नयां �मल कर राष्ट्रप�त भवन गए। मुझे बड़े दु:ख \nके साथ कहना पड़ता है �क जो मैडल इन फौजी भाइय� को बहादुर� के �लए �मले थे, वे उन्ह�ने वापस \nकर �दए। यह इस�लए हुआ क्य��क �पछले दो मह�ने से हमारे एक्स-स�वर्समैन धरने पर जन्तर-मन्तर \nपर ब ै ठे थे और उनक� �डमांड थी, \"One Rank - One Pay\". यह �कतनी अजीब बात है �क एक \nतरफ सारा दे श �डफ� स स�वर्�सज़ क� तरफ ध्यान दे ता है �क हमार� फौजी ताकत मज़बूत हो और दूसर� \nतरफ वे फौजी ह�, िजन्ह�ने हमेशा अपने दे श के �लए जान� द�ं, ले�कन उनक� तरफ सरकार का ध्यान \nनह�ं है। \nसर, हमारे दे श म� 35 लाख एक्स-स�वर्समैन ह�, िजनम� से तक़र�बन 19 लाख जवान ह�। यह बात \nसभी को पता है �क हमारे फौिजय� क� �रटायरम�ट early age म � होती है। फौज का जवान 40 वषर् \nक� एज म� �रटायर होता है और जो कनर्ल और �ब्रगे�डयर ह�, वे 50 और 55 क� ऐज म� �रटायर होते \nह�। जब उनको अल� ऐज म� �रटायर �कया जाता है, तब उन्ह� प�शन के �सवाए और कु छ नह�ं �मलता, \nले�कन हुआ क्या है �क िजतनी बार भी सरकार ने प�शन के क े �सज़ के �लए रूल्स बनाए ह�, अन्य सब \nस�वर्�सज़ के �लए तो प्रावधान कर �दया गया, ले�कन एक्स-स�वर्समैन के �लए कु छ भी नह�ं �कया गया। \nइ स के कारण हुआ यह है �क �डफर�ट स्टे�सज़ पर जो स�वर्समैन �रटायर हुए, उनको �डफर�ट त र � के से \nप�शन �मल रह� है। कह�ं पर कनर्ल क� प�शन ज्यादा है तो मेजर जनरल क� कम है, कह�ं हवलदार क� \nज्यादा है तो उ स के ऑ�फसर क� प�शन कम है। \nसर, म� आ प के माध्यम से सरकार का ध्यान इस ओर �दलाना चाहता हूं �क अगर एक्स-स�वर्समैन \nनाराज़ रहे, तो इसका असर स�व�ग सोल्जसर् पर भी पड़ता है, इस�लए सरकार को जल्द से जल्द इनक� \n�डमांड्स को पूरा करना चा�हए। इनक� �डमांड्स बहुत �सम्पल है �क सभी को एक जैसा ट्र�ट �कया जाए, \nजैसा �क बाक� स�वर्�सज़ म� �कया जाता है। हम� समझ म� नह�ं आता �क इस इश्यू पर यह सरकार चुप \nक्य� बैठ� है, जब�क सारे दे श का ध्यान हमार� आम� क� तरफ है। आम� क� मज़बूती के साथ दे श क� \nमज़बूती है। हम इन सब फौिजय� को सड़क� पर घूमते दे ख कर क्य� मौन ह�? वे अपने मैडल्स वापस \nकर रहे ह�। धन्यवाद। \nश्रीमती वृंदा कारत (पिश्चमी बंगाल): सर, म� इ न के साथ इस �वषय पर स्वयं को एसो�सएट करती \nहूं। \nश्री अव�न राय (पिश्चमी बंगाल): सर, म� भी इन्ह� एसो�सएट करता हूं। \nश्री राम नारायण साहू (उत्तर प्रदे श): सर, म� स्वयं को इ न के �वषय से एसो�सएट करता हूं। \nConstruction of old age homes \nश्री प्रभात झा (मध्य प्रदे श): सर, सामािजक न्याय एवं अ�धका�रता मंत्रालय के इश्तहार हम रोज \nदे खते ह� और इश्तहार� म� आता है �क वृद्ध� के �लए वृद्धाश्रम बनाए जाने के �लए सरकार बहुत काम कर \nरह� है, ले�कन �पछले �दन� यह मामला सामने आया है �क वृद्धाश्रम बनाने के �लए के न् द्र सरकार क� जो \nयोजना है, उसका सारा बजट बंद कर �दया है और उस मंत्रालय के मंत्री के नाम से ह� यह बयान छपा \n\n345 \nहै। मेरा कहना यह है यह दे श वृद्ध� का सम्मान करता है और इ स के �लए सरकार क� कु छ योजनाएं ह�। \nस्वयं आपने ह� कहा है �क वृद्धाश्रम बनाने के �लए पैसे �दए जाएंगे। \nहद तो तब हो गई, जब एक एनजीओ को मंत्रालय का पत्र पहुंचा �क ये जो सार� योजनाएं ह�, अब \nये गैर योजनाओं म� आ गई ह�, इस�लए आपको कोई भी पैसा नह�ं �मलेगा। क्या सरकार वृद्ध� का इसी \nतरह  सम्मान करती  \n\n346 \nहै? आज तक मेर� समझ म� यह नह�ं आया �क सम्मान का यह कौन सा तर�का है? इतना ह� नह�ं, \nसरकार आधे-आधे पेज का इश्तहार छापती है �क हम वृद्ध� का सम्मान करती है। म� सरकार से इस \nसम्बंध म� जानकार� चाहता हूं और यह चाहता हूं �क कम से कम वृद्ध� के सम्मान के �लए सरकार अपने \nबजट म� प्रावधान रखना प्रारम्भ करे, अन्यथा �फर वह इस प्रकार के इश्तहार छापना और झूठे बयान \nदे ना बंद करे । \nSuicide by Farmers in Vidharba Region \nश्री प्रकाश जावडेकर (महाराष्ट्र): उपसभाप�त महोदय, नया साल शुरु हुए आज 43 �दन हो गए ह� \nऔर इन 43 �दन� म� क्या हुआ, तो महाराष्ट्र के �वदभर् र�ज़न म� 103 �कसान� ने आत्महत्या क�। 103 \nsuicides in 43 days और यह सरकार क� इस घोषणा के बाद हुआ �क सब के कज� माफ हो गए \nह�। कजर् माफ क्य� �कए थे, यह बताकर �क �कसान आत्महत्या कर रहा है। उसको आत्महत्या से बचाने \nके �लए यह कजर् माफ� क� घोषणा हमने क� है। इ स के �लए हमने 70 हजार करोड़ रुपए �दए ह�। \nले�कन, वास्त�वकता यह है �क जो �कसान आत्महत्या कर रहे ह�, उनम� से 10 फ�सद� �कसान� को भी \nकजर्-माफ� का लाभ नह�ं हुआ है क्य��क इन्ह�ने जो कं ड ी श ं स डाले - हमने मांग क� थी �क हर �कसान \nका 50 हजार रुपए तक का कजर् माफ हो, ले�कन इस सरकार ने यह नह�ं सुना। कहा गया �क 5 एकड़ \nसे ज्यादा भू�म रखने वाले �कसान को कजर्-माफ� नह�ं �मलेगी। �वदभर् म� अगर बाप के िजंदा रहते उ स के \nतीन बेटे अलग-अलग खेती करते ह�, तो उनका जो टाइटल है, वह �डवाइड नह�ं होता है और इस�लए \nउसक� भू�म 5 एकड़ से ज्यादा �दखती है। ले�कन, \nिजनक� dry land farming है, िजनक� \nirrigation नह�ं है, वहां भी 5 एकड़ से ज्यादा जमीन है, उनको माफ� नह�ं �मल� है। िजसने एक \nभी �कश्त भर�, one instalment repaid, the honest farmer is punished. उसको  \nकजर्-माफ� का लाभ नह�ं �मला है। जो प्राइवेट मनी ल� �ड ंग है उसको institutional lending म� \nconvert करो, हमार� यह मांग भी सरकार ने स्वीकार नह�ं क�, इस�लए आज कजर्-माफ� का लाभ \n10 फ�सद� �कसान� को भी नह�ं �मला है और �कसान मरने पर उतारु है, आत्महत्या कर रहा है। \nदूसर� चीज़ यह है �क जो कपास उगाता है, तो कपास के �लए �म�नमम सपोटर् प्राइस 3 हजार रुपए \nहै, ले�कन 3 हजार रुपए �म�नमम सपोटर् प्राइस म� आज वे बेच नह�ं रहे ह� क्य��क Cotton \nCorporation म� और NAFED म� खर�द-बंद के �लए महाराष्ट्र सरकार ने अपनी योजना भी बंद कर \nद�। वह आज 2300-2400 म� कपास बेचने पर मजबूर है, ले�कन उनका cost of production \nनह�ं �नकल रहा है और इ स के कारण आज वह कं ग ा ल है, आत्महत्या के कगार पर है। यह 103 लोग \nमरे ह�, के व ल ऐसा ह� नह�ं है, बिल्क कजर्-माफ� क� घोषणा के अमल के बाद 1300 �कसान� ने �वदभर् \nम� आत्महत्या क� है। ऐसे ह� हजार� क� संख्या म� आंध्र म� भी आत्महत्या हुई ह�। दोन� कांग्रेस-रूल्ड \nस्टेट्स ह�। राज्य सरकार� कु छ नह�ं कर रह� ह� और के न् द्र सरकार भी कु छ नह�ं कर रह� है। ...(समय \nक� घंट�)... इस�लए म� यह कहूंगा �क �कसान के साथ जो सबसे बड़ा धोखा हुआ है, वह यह है �क \nकजर्-माफ� का कु छ भी फायदा उसे नह�ं �मला है। जब �कसान MSP के नीचे अपना उत्पाद बेचने को \nमजबूर है तब वह एक �क्र�मनल ऑफ� स होना चा�हए, जो �क आज नह�ं हो रहा है और इस�लए आज \n�कसान मर रहा है, आत्महत्या कर रहा है। इस सरकार क� भत्सर्ना करते हुए म� इस �वषय पर अपनी \nबात समाप्त करता हूं। \n\n347 \nLiberalization of F.D.I. Guidelines \nSHRI MOINUL HASSAN (West Bengal): Sir, the Congress Government has \ntaken an outrageous step in liberalizing the Foreign Direct Investment \nguidelines. At one stroke, across the board,  \nthe  sectoral  caps  on  FDI  have  been  nullified  by  excluding  \ninvestments by companies \"owned or  \n\n348 \ncontrolled\" by Indians having substantial foreign capital. By this \nredefinition, FDI can be routed through \"Indian companies\" and not be \nclassified as FDI. \nBy this sleigh of hand, there will be no sectoral cap on FDI in \ntelecom, Defence, aviation, media, etc. Even in the retail sector, FDI \ncan make a backdoor entry through these guidelines. In the insurance \nsector, the present cap of 26 per cent can be subverted. This is a device \nto bypass Parliament where a legislation to amend the law to increase the \ncap in insurance is pending. \nWhile doing this, at the end of the present Government's tenure, the \nGovernment would like to ensure backdoor entry of FDI virtually in all \nsectors without limits. \nIn view of this, I would say that the Government has shown its utter \ncontempt for Parliament by announcing these new guidelines on the eve of \nthe Parliament Session. Sir, it is nothing but they are bent upon eroding \nthe economic sovereignty of the country. So, in this perspective, I would \nlike to demand the rescinding of new guidelines immediately. \nSHRIMATI BRINDA KARAT (West Bengal): Sir, I associate myself with what \nthe hon. Member, Shri Moinul Hassan, has said. ...(Interruptions)... \nSHRI PRASANTA CHATTERJEE (West Bengal): Sir, I associate myself with \nwhat the hon. Member, Shri Moinul Hassan, has said. ...(Interruptions)... \nSHRI SAMAN PATHAK (West Bengal): Sir, I associate myself with what the \nhon. Member, Shri Moinul Hassan, has said. \nMR. DEPUTY CHAIRMAN: Okay, it's ail right. ...(Interruptions)... Only \nassociate please, nothing else. Now, Special Mentions. \n...(Interruptions)... I have called the other Member and have taken up \nthe other subject. ...(Interruptions)... Nothing else will go on record. \n...(Interruptions)... Let us not break the rules. ...(Interruptions)... \nSHRI PRASANTA CHATTERJEE: Sir, we want a discussion \n...(Interruptions)... \nश्री उपसभाप�त: आप बै�ठए। ...(व्यवधान)... बैठ जाइए। Nothing will go on record. \n...(Interruptions)... \n_____________ \n\n349 \nSPECIAL MENTIONS \nNeed to give House No. 100, Lodhi Estate, New Delhi to Ch. Devi Lal Trust \nSARDAR TARLOCHAN SINGH (Haryana): Sir, with your permission, I am \nraising this issue. I have raised this matter earlier also on a number of \noccasions, but no results have yielded so far. Now, again, I am \npresenting before the House the matter relating to according due honour \nto the former Deputy Prime Minister Ch. Devi Lal. A number of times, \nthrough special mentions and questions,  this  matter  had  been  raised \nin the House, but the Ministry has kept stoic silence on this  \n\n350 \nimportant issue. All the hon. Members of the House are aware about the \npatriotic role of Ch. Devi Lal, who, in spite of being from the family of \nleading agriculturist, joined the Freedom Movement at an early age.  He \nremained in jail for a number of years and never bothered for the \natrocities committed against his family by the British Government. He was \nresponsible for a major achievement of his life when Haryana was created \nas a separate State in 1966. He remained the Chief Minister of Haryana \nfor a number of times. In 1989, Ch. Devi Lal was unanimously elected as \nthe Prime Minister of India but he refused to accept the honour and \nnominated Shri V.P.Singh, in his place, as Prime Minister. This sacrifice \nof the highest post in the country is an unparallel gesture by any \nindividual. He remained the Deputy Prime Minister of the country twice. \nHe was a Member of Rajya Sabha at the time of his death. \nThe Government of India should have given the House No. 100, Lodhi \nEstate, New Delhi, where he lived and died, to Ch. Devi Lal Trust for \nestablishing a museum on his life, deeds and to propagate the ideals for \nwhich he lived his life. I, once again, make a strong plea that the Urban \nDevelopment Minister may agree to this as he has done in few other cases. \nश्री रुद्रनारायण पा�ण: सर, हालां�क अंग्रेजी म� बोला गया, �फर भी म� इससे संबद्ध करता हूं। \nNeed to consult local authorities before implementing the notification  \non coastal zone regulation \nSHRI N. BALAGANGA (Tamil Nadu): The Government has issued the draft \nCoastal Management Zone (CMS) Notification 2008 on 1st May 2008 and, \nagain, on 21st July 2008. The present Notification 2008 intends to \nreplace the existing Coastal Regulation Zone (CRZ) Notification of \nFebruary, 1991 that has already been amended 19 times in the past 17 \nyears and replace it with the new one to manage the country's 7,500 km \nlong coastline. The proposed notification is being advocated without \ntaking into account the livelihood issues of local people and it has \nalready become contentious with fishing and coastal communities \nprotesting the Government's move. With the Notification available only in \nEnglish and Hindi, the communities living along the coast are not able to \nunderstand the draft. Since most people, especially the fishing \ncommunities cannot understand the contents of the document, there is a \nneed to translate the draft CMZ notification into languages of the \n\n351 \ncommunities living along the coast. Environmental activists have pointed \nout that the Government had not interacted with the local panchayats to \nspread awareness on the notification. They apprehend that the new zone \nclassifications will pave the way for proliferation of Special Economic \nZones, ports, tourist resorts, mining and similar other activities along \nlarge areas of the coast. I, therefore, request the Centre not to impose \nsuch a notification without consulting local authorities who would be \ndirectly affected and who would have to implement the guidelines on the \nground. The basic purpose of notification of the CRZ 1991 did not serve \nwell due to improper implementation. The implementation mechanism \nstipulated in the present CMZ is also very vague. Thank you, Sir. \n\n352 \nDR. K. MALAISAMY (Tamil Nadu): Sir, I associate myself with the \nSpecial Mention made by the hon. Member. \nMR. DEPUTY CHAIRMAN: Shri Lalit Kishore Chaturvedi. Absent. The House \nstands adjourned till 2.00 p.m. \nThe House then adjourned for lunch at fifty six minutes past twelve of \nthe clock. \nThe House re-assembled after lunch at One minute past two of the clock. \nRE. DEMAND FOR INFORMATION TO BE GIVEN BY THE HOME MINISTER \nTHE VICE-CHAIRMAN (SHRI PRASANTA CHATTERJEE) in the Chair. \nश्रीमती सुषमा स्वराज (मध्य प्रदे श): महोदय, जीरो ऑवर के दौरान नेता प्र�तप� ने श्री यशवंत \n�सन्हा जी क� बेरहम �पटाई के �वषय को उठाया था, तब गृह मंत्री जी ने कहा था �क उनक े पास अभी \n�कसी तथ्य क� जानकार� नह�ं है, न वे कु छ स्वीकार कर सकते ह�, न नकार सकते ह�। हम लोग� को \nपता था �क 2:00 बजे हाऊस जब दोबारा �मलेगा, तो गृह मंत्री यहां उपिस्थत होकर जरूर हम लोग� \nको सूचना द�गे, जानकार� उनक े पास तब तक आ चुक� होगी, ले�कन गृह मंत्री तो सदन म� �दखाई भी \nनह�ं दे रहे ह�। तो म� पा�लर्याम�ट्र� अफ े यर �म�नस्टर से पूछना चाहती हूं �क क्या गृह मंत्री अभी आ रहे \nह� और वे हम लोग� को सूचना और जानकार� द�गे? क्य��क, नेता प्र�तप� ने जो �वषय उठाया था, \nउसका सबब बहुत बड़ा है, वह के व ल एक सांसद क� �पटाई का मामला नह�ं है। \n...(Interruptions)... \nTHE VICE- CHAIRMAN (SHRI PRASANTA CHATTERJEE): Now, as per the \nscheduled agenda, the Interim Budget (Railway), 2009-10 will be placed by \nShri Lalu Prasad. ...(Interruptions)... \nश्रीमती सुषमा स्वराज: उपसभाध्य� जी, मेर� बात का आप जवाब क्य� नह�ं दे रहे ह�? \n...(व्यवधान)... मेर� बात का जवाब द�िजए। ...(व्यवधान).... \nश्री एस. एस. अहलुवा�लया (झारखंड): महोदय, जब तक गृह मंत्री यहां उपिस्थत नह�ं होते, तब \nतक सदन क� कायर्वाह� स्थ�गत क� जाए। ...(व्यवधान)... \nTHE VICE*CHAIRMAN (SHRI PRASANTA CHATTERJEE): Now, Shri Lalu Prasad \nwill lay the Interim Budget (Railway), 2009-10 \n_____________ \nTHE INTERIM BUDGET (RAILWAYS), 2009-10 \nरे ल मंत्री (श्री लालू प्रसाद): महोदय, म� रे लवे के संबंध म� 2009-10 के वषर् के �लए भारत सरकार \nक� अनुमा�नत प्रािप्तय� और व्यय का �ववरण (अंग्रेजी तथा �हन्द� म�) सभा पटल पर रखता हूं। \n...(व्यवधान)... \n\n353 \nTHE VICE-CHAIRMAN (SHRI PRASANTA CHATTERJEE): Now, the hon. Railway \nMinister will lay the Supplementary Demands for Grants (Railways), 2008-\n09 \n_____________ \n\n354 \nSUPPLEMENTARY DEMANDS FOR GRANTS (RAILWAYS) 2008-09 \nरे ल मंत्री (श्री लालू प्रसाद): महोदय, म� 2008-09 के वषर् के �लए अनुपूरक अनुदान मांग� (रे ल) \nको दशार्ने वाला एक �ववरण (अंग्रेजी तथा �हन्द� म�) सभा पटल पर रखता हूं। ...(व्यवधान)... \n_____________ \nRE. DEMAND FOR IMFORMATION TO BE GIVEN BY THE HOME MINISTER – Contd. \nश्री एस. एस. अहलुवा�लया: महोदय, इस सदन के एक माननीय सदस्य के साथ िजस तरह से \nपु�लस ने दुव्यर्वहार �कया, िजस तरह से मार-पीट क� और �गरफ्तार करने के बावजूद यहां पर सू�चत \nनह�ं �कया गया, यह इस सदन क� अवहेलना है, इस सदन का अपमान है। ...(व्यवधान)... \nTHE VICE-CHAIRMAN (SHRI PRASANT CHATTERJEE): The House is adjourned up \nto 2.30 p.m. \nThe House then adjourned at three minutes past two of the clock. \nThe House reassembled at thirty minutes past two of the clock, \n(MR. DEPUTY CHAIRMAN in the Chair.) \nPRIVATE MEMBERS' BILLS \nMR. DEPUTY CHAIRMAN: Private Members' Bills. Dr. Murli Manohar Joshi. \nNot present. Shri Shantaram Laxrnan Naik. \nThe Constitution (Amendment) Bill, 2008 (To amend the S eventh \nSchedule) \nSHRI SHANTARAM LAXMAN NAIK (Goa): Sir, I move for leave to introduce a \nBill further to amend the Constitution of India. \nThe question was put and the motion was adopted. \nSHRI SHANTARAM LAXMAN NAIK: Sir, I introduce the Bill. \n_____________ \nThe Constitution (Amendment) Bill, 2008 (To amend Article, 145) \nSHRI SHANTARAM LAXMAN NAIK (Goa): Sir, I move for leave to introduce a \nBill further to amend the Constitution of India. \nThe question was put and the motion was adopted. \nSHRI SHANTARAM LAXMAN NAIK: Sir, I introduce the Bill. \n_____________ \nThe Passports (Amendment) Bill, 2008 (To amend Section 5) \nSHRI SHANTARAM LAXMAN NAIK (Goa): Sir, I move for leave to introduce a \nBill further to amend the Passports Act, 1967. \nThe question was put and the motion was adopted. \nSHRI SHANTARAM LAXMAN NAIK: Sir, I introduce the Bill. \nMR. DEPUTY CHAIRMAN: Shri Rajeev Chandrasekhar; not present. Dr. \nAbhishek Manu Singhvi; not present. Shri Kalraj Mishra. \n\n355 \n_____________ \n\n356 \nThe Compulsory Medical Treatment in Emergency Condition and to Women in \nLabour by Private Hospitals and Medical Practioners Bill, 2008 \nश्री कलराज �मश्र (उत्तर प्रदे श्): महोदय, म� प्रस्ताव करता हूं �क �नजी अस्पताल� और �च�कत्सा \nव्यवसा�यय� द्वारा आपात �च�कत्सा और प्रसव पीड़ा क� िस्थ�त म� म�हलाओं के �लए अ�नवायर् �च�कत्सा \nउपचार और तत्संसक्त अथवा उ स के आनुषं�गक �वषय� का उपबंध करने के �लए एक �वधेयक को \nपुर:स्था�पत करने क� अनुम�त द� जाए। \nThe question was put and the motion was adopted. \nश्री कलराज �मश्र: महोदय, म� �वधेयक को पुर:स्था�पत करता हूं। \n_____________ \nThe Electricity (Amendment) Bill, 2008 \nSHRI PRAKASH JAVADEKAR (Maharashtra): Sir, I move for leave to \nintroduce a Bill further to amend the Electricity Bill, 2003. \nThe question was put and the motion was adopted. \nSHRI PRAKASH JAVADEKAR: Sir, I introduce the Bill. \n_____________ \nThe Medical Termination of Pregnancy (Amendment) Bill, 2008 \nSHRI PRAKASH JAVADEKAR (Maharashtra): Sir, I move for leave to \nintroduce a Bill further to amend the Medical Termination of Pregnancy \nAct, 1971. \nThe question was put and the motion was adopted. \nSHRI PRAKASH JAVADEKAR: Sir, I introduce the Bill. \n_____________ \nThe Medicare Service Persons and Medicare Service Institutions  \n(Protection from violence and damage to property) Bill, 2008 \nSHRI PRAKASH JAVADEKAR (Maharashtra): Sir, I move for leave to \nintroduce a Bill to protect the medicare service persons and medicare \nservice institutions from violence and damage to property and impose \npunishment on the offender and for matter connected therewith and \nincidental thereto. \nThe question was put and the motion was adopted. \nSHRI PRAKASH JAVADEKAR: Sir, I introduce the Bill. \n_____________ \nThe Acts of Parliament (Application to Nagaland) Bill, 2009 \nSHRI KHEKIHO ZHIMOMI (Nagaland): Sir, I move for leave to introduce a \nBill to provide for the procedure for application of the Acts of \nParliament in respect of the State of Nagaland and for matters connected \ntherewith. \n\n357 \nThe question was put and the motion was adopted. \nSHRI KHEKIHO ZHIMOMI: Sir, I introduce the Bill. \n\n358 \nMR. DEPUTY CHAIRMAN: Shri Mahendra Mohan to move for leave to \nintroduce three Bills. Absent. \n_____________ \nThe Constitution (Scheduled Castes) Order (Amendment) Bill, 2009 \nSHRIMATI VIPLOVE THAKUR (Himachal Pradesh): Sir, I move for leave to \nintroduce a Bill to further amend the Constitution (Scheduled Castes) \nOrder, 1950. \nThe question was put and the motion was adopted. \nSHRIMATI VIPLOVE THAKUR: Sir, I introduce the Bill. \n_____________ \nMR. DEPUTY CHAIRMAN: We shall now take up further consideration of the \nCompulsory Voting and Pre- Poll Survey and Exit Poll of Elections Bill, \n2004. Shri Raashid Alvi to continue. He is not there. \nThe Compulsory Voting and Prohibition of pre-poll survey and  \nexit poll of Elections Bill, 2004 - Contd. \nTHE MINISTER OF LAW AND JUSTICE (SHRI H. R. BHARDWAJ): Sir, I think a \nlot of debate has gone on this issue. We had discussed this issue for \ntwo-three days. Hon. Members from both sides of the House have been very \nimpressive indeed. We are aware of the complexity of the question. \nReforms in the electoral process are always introduced after a consensus \namongst all political parties. Considering the importance of this matter, \nI think we must refer it to the Standing Committee of this Ministry. \nAfter the Report of the Standing Committee is obtained, as in the case of \nother matters received from the Election Commission for the consideration \nof the Committee recently, I wish this also could be discussed at length. \nAnd if there is a consensus amongst all political parties, then such a \nprovision of compulsory voting could be introduced. At this stage, this \ndiscussion has been very healthy and fruitful. The hon. Member is now the \nMinister. So, it is no longer a Private Member's Bill. I request that \nthis Biff be withdrawn.  \nMR. DEPUTY CHAIRMAN: Mr. Narayanasamy is not here. \n...(Interruptions)... No, he is not replying. ...(Interruptions)... \nSHRI H.R. BHARDWAJ: Every Member has spoken on this Bill. Therefore, \nit is the property of the House now. \nMR. DEPUTY CHAIRMAN: I shall now put the motion for consideration to \nvote. \nThe question is: \n \"That the Bill to provide for compulsory voting by the voters in an \nelection called for by the Election Commission and to prohibit pre-\npoll survey and exit poll by various agencies and on their printing, \n\n359 \npublication and telecasting through the print and electronic media so \nas to remove the confusion of the electorate and for matters connected \ntherewith and incidental thereto, be taken into consideration\". \nThe question was put and the motion was negatived. \n_____________ \n\n360 \nThe Voluntary Organizations Regulatory Authority Bill, 2006 \nश्री कलराज �मश्र (उत्तर प्रदे श): माननीय उपसभाप�त महोदय, स्वैिच्छक संगठन �व�नयामक \nप्रा�धकरण �वधेयक जो हमने 2006 म� प्रस्तुत �कया था, आज उ स के ऊपर चचार् करने का अवसर \nउपलब्ध हुआ है। आपने अनुम�त द� है, इ स के �लए म� आपका अत्य�धक आभार� हूं। मान्यवर, जो \n�वधेयक प्रस्तुत �कया गया है, इ स के प ी छे �वशेष उद्देश्य है और उस उद्देश्य को हमने बड़ा स्पष्ट रूप से \nइसम� प्रस्तुत �कया है। और म� चाहूंगा �क एक बार उद्देश्य सामने आ जाए तो स्वयंमेव पता चलेगा �क \nइस प्रा�धकरण �वधेयक क� आवश्यकता क्य� पड़ी। आज स्वयंसेवी संगठन समाज का एक अ�भन्न अंग \nहै। समग्र समाज और दे श के �वकास म� इन संगठन� ने काफ� योगदान �कया है। वे �व�भन्न �ेत्र� म� \nसरकार के कायर्कलाप� म� सहायक होते ह� और संकट तथा प्राकृ �तक आपदाओं के समय ये स्वयंसेवी \nसंगठन ईश्वर�य कृ त्य� से प्रभा�वत लोग� को राहत प्रदान करते ह� और उनका बचाव करते ह�। ये \nस्वयंसेवी संगठन �श�ा, स्वास्थ्य, द ेखर ेख उपलब्ध कराते ह� और अनाथ बच्च� के �लए अनाथालय और \nवृद्धाश्रम भी चला रहे ह� तथा जरूरतमंद लोग� को भोजन और दवा उपलब्ध करा रहे ह�। अनेक स्वयंसेवी \nसंगठन मुख्यत: अंशदान और दान के माध्यम से प्राप्त �न�धय� पर �नभर्र करते ह�, जो उनक े व्यय को \nपूरा करने के �लए पयार्प्त नह�ं होती। इस�लए ऐसे अ�धकांश संगठन� के �लए अनेक कायर्कलाप� के \n�नष्पादन म� �न�धय� का अभाव रहता है। भारत म� लगभग दस लाख स्वयंसेवी संगठन पंजीकृ त ह�, \nिजनम� सत्रह हजार एक स� प�ता�लस स्वयंसेवी संगठन� को �वदे श� से �न�धयां प्राप्त हो रह� है। इन \nस्वयंसेवी संगठन� म� बढ़ती प्र�तस्पद्धार् के कारण ये अपना अिस्तत्व बनाए रखने के �लए �नयम� को तोड़ \nरहे ह� तथा कानून का उल्लंघन कर रहे ह�। हाल ह� म� कु छ ऐसी अ�नय�मतताएं जानकार� म� आई ह�, \nिजसम� कई स्वयंसेवी संगठन� ने �वदे शी मुद्रा प्रबंध अ�ध�नयम का उल्लंघन �कया है, िजनक े कई दे श� \nम� धन तथा ब�क खाते पाए गए ह�। 2005 म� गृह मंत्रालय ने �वदे शी मुद्रा प्रबंधन अ�ध�नयम का \nउल्लंघन करने पर आठ हजार छ: सौ �तहत्तर गैर सरकार� संगठन� को काल� सूची म� डाल �दया\n है। \nइ स के अलावा अनुदान �वतरण के संबंध म� �व�भन्न सरकार� �वभाग� म� भाई-भतीजावाद के कई मामले \nदे खने को �मले ह�। यह उल्लेख �कया गया है �क कई �वभाग� म� अनुदान प्रदान करने वाले व्यिक्त ह� \nपरो� रूप से स्वयंसेवी संगठन� के मा�लक होते ह�। इस�लए अनुदान प्राप्त करना बहुत क�ठन हो जाता \nहै, क्य��क वास्त�वक संगठन� को परोपकार के प्रयोजनाथर् वां�छत अनुदान प्राप्त करने के �लए अनेक \nव्यिक्तय� को तुष्ट करने म� �दक्कत� आती ह�। के न् द्र तथा राज्य� के स्तर पर सरकार� द्वारा उन्ह� धन \nउपलब्ध कराया जाता है। �कन्तु इस धन का